  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a reader, I want to jump to any page from the page number in the title, so that I move in long topics quickly.\n\n### Scope\n\n'Aller à la page…', first/last, ±5 around current, blocks of 50, all pages up to 30; next-page cue at the end of a page.\n\n- Module: App · Difficulty: easy · Priority: high · post-MVP\n- Implements: FEAT-002 (#146)\n- Absorbs: FEAT-002; legacy backlog HFR-008 (end-of-page cue)\n- Legacy sources (read-only, `origin/master`): legacy 4.0 'last 3 pages' picker and topic menu (`MessagesView.swift`)\n- Spec: `docs/features/FEAT-002.md` (feature spec, ADR 0011 §2; write it first if absent, crediting Bybifok) plus a short `docs/lots/LOT-110-*.md` pointing to it\n\n### Depends on\n\n- LOT-083 (#101, done)\n- LOT-033 (#60, done)\n\n### Blocked by\n\nnone: every dependency is merged (unblocked 2026-10-29, steward ext/opus-helper1)\n\n### Feature umbrella\n\n- Implements FEAT-002 (#146), proposed by Bybifok (credit in the spec, PR and CREDITS.md). Other lots of this feature: none; **this lot is the last one: its PR also says `Closes #146`**.\n\nFEAT issues (#145–#165) are umbrellas and are never claimed: claim this lot's issue; the PR says `Closes #<this issue>` and `Refs #<FEAT issue>`.\n\n### Model\n\nSonnet → Opus (AGENTS.md §6: the reviewer is never the author model)\n\n### Captures needed\n\n- none known; any page state the spec needs and the fixtures lack is listed as *pending capture*, never hand-built (LESSONS 35-36)\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Out-of-range input refused; the page HFR serves is shown (LOT-082 rule).\n- [ ] View logic lives in `@Observable @MainActor` models tested with Swift Testing in `App/SwiftHFRTests/`; each new test is shown to fail without the change.\n- [ ] `xcodebuild build test` green on the iPhone 18 Pro and an iPad simulator (iOS 27.0), and the `App build + tests` CI job green.\n- [ ] UI strings in French; light, dark and Dynamic Type XL checked; no new dependency; no HFR fact without a source (legacy file:line or fixture).\n\n### Before you start (agents and humans)\n\nRead, in order: AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, docs/agents/ORCHESTRATION.md, docs/agents/REVIEW-ROUNDS.md, docs/agents/LESSONS.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, docs/ARCHITECTURE.md, App/README.md, ADR 0012, the spec of every dependency (docs/lots/), docs/HFR-PROTOCOL.md for any forum fact, docs/FIXTURES.md if captures are involved. Claim with `/claim <session-id>` on this issue before writing code; PR body `Closes #<this issue>` + `Claim: <session-id>`; never guess HFR behaviour (stop and list the captures needed).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
